    "check": "returned unopposed: the eight nominations named in the Banbridge Chronicle of 8 May 1964, p. 1 (two newcomers and 'the other six are sitting members'; read on the BNA page image), 'only eight nominations ... for the nine seats' (Banbridge Chronicle, 5 June 1964, p. 1), and the new council met on 26 May 1964 with Pantridge and Wilkinson welcomed as new members (Ulster Star, 30 May 1964, p. 20)",
