  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore Urban District Council, nine seats; urban polling day 20 May 1964. There was no poll: only eight nominations were received for the nine seats (Banbridge Chronicle, 8 May and 5 June 1964). The ninth seat went to the retiring member James Russell, who agreed to continue for a further term: with too few nominations a retiring member was deemed re-elected, so he is recorded with the eight. Printed 'Capt. Robert Johnston, Messrs. Joseph Gibson, J.P.; Thomas Castles, John McGrehan, Alex. Russell and Douglas Gamble' as the six sitting members renominated. Only eight nominations were received for the nine seats; the ninth went to the retiring member James Russell, who had not sought re-election but agreed to continue for a further term, a retiring member deemed re-elected (Banbridge Chronicle, 5 June 1964, p. 1). Returned unopposed."
